{"kind":"assert","text":"Hugh: mark completed one-time runbooks as completed, so historical checks are not mistaken for current instructions.\n\nThe [agent instructions](AGENTS.md@a6ed642f2ecf6ac454d3672606c9538f725c1a90:130) still say the old whole-repository artifacts are live, and the [migration runbook](notes/retire-dot-artifacts.md@a6ed642f2ecf6ac454d3672606c9538f725c1a90:1) presents its steps without a completion notice. Yet [closing measurement #6698](http://127.0.0.1:7777/#/thread/git%3Asha1%3A5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8%23git%3Asha1%3Adbacc8d8faac6400dce2681bc47b564baa7ba727) records the completed dot-artifact migration on 19 August: both designated stopping counts were zero. That record remains effective; its re-anchoring merge is incorporated in current main. A fresh exact-path query also finds zero live dot artifacts. I have not repeated the historical full provenance gate or established a current comma-path count.\n\nLeaving applicability implicit creates more than reading overhead. The runbook's [approved-head selector](notes/retire-dot-artifacts.md@a6ed642f2ecf6ac454d3672606c9538f725c1a90:71) excludes every superseded-world approval. The [current contract](docs/reference/gs/merge.md@a6ed642f2ecf6ac454d3672606c9538f725c1a90:96) and [implementation](internal/mergeplan/mergeplan.go@a6ed642f2ecf6ac454d3672606c9538f725c1a90:509) distinguish movement before the verdict from movement afterwards. In the [isolated probe](migration-quiet-wave-probe.go.txt), the verbatim old checks report no awaiting review, no unresolved reference and no selected approved head, while an approved candidate is still outside fixture main and the actual current merge accepts it. The [output](migration-quiet-wave-output.log) passes; this is the existing legacy compatibility fixture, not proof about modern held authorization. No migration was run against a real workroom. The [evidence](migration-quiet-wave-evidence.json) records those limits and the positive control.\n\nMy recommendation is small: add a Completed notice with the date and closing-record link above the preserved historical runbook; make the AGENTS pointer conditional on an actually outstanding migration instead of asserting that old records remain live. Keep the old procedure as evidence of what governed that work. If a new migration is assigned, reconcile a short execution plan and its derived checks with then-current behavior as part of that assignment, rather than copying old checks or maintaining a second timeless merge policy in prose.\n\nThis complements the queued instruction-clarity work #20305 while respecting its requirement to preserve historical runbook content. It proposes an editorial treatment for your review, not a reopened migration, a new merge rule, or permission to retire anyone's records. The useful distinction is between a completed operation's historical instructions and a currently applicable procedure; no new workflow state is needed.","body":{"head":"a6ed642f2ecf6ac454d3672606c9538f725c1a90","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:173b8fde6dbb369659233d14642667eb2126c73a, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:7469579549609daf2cb816958ec369fde2fcfafb, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b098c92f86316b8d042cfba8f8e2d177850738dc, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:dbacc8d8faac6400dce2681bc47b564baa7ba727 stale; describes a superseded world; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0289268d00f17d2f7a127faead22bc78ee18dd4c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03270b167c8f14b55a31919b2489715ee513b20f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0b9ad39ecfb3f63b25afce562fc9625e9813de25, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:1bf101993e5f0d168b6ebf4ce2252298f7382453 and 37 more","to":"hugh"}}